        "original_id": "1c0f1020-12f9-5d51-8a37-3e5440f64632",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Netaji Bhawan, Kolkata\n- People: Subhas Chandra Bose\n- Organizations: Nazi Germany, Imperial Japan\n- Topics: Indian nationalism, World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Subhas Chandra Bose was born on 23 January 1897 and died on 18 August 1945.\n- Subhas Chandra Bose was an Indian nationalist whose defiant patriotism made him a hero in India.\n- During World War II, Subhas Chandra Bose tried to free India from British rule with help from Nazi Germany and Imperial Japan, which left a troubled legacy.\n- Netaji Bhawan, also called Netaji Bhavan, is a building in Kolkata maintained as a memorial and research center dedicated to the life of Subhas Chandra Bose.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
